---
title: Recovering a message from a crashed consumer (leases and the reaper)
---
sequenceDiagram
    %% SQL: CLAIM_SQL, RENEW_LEASE_SQL, REAP_SQL, ACK_SQL in app/broker/messages.py.
    %% Heartbeats: app/worker.py. Reaper: app/reaper.py (runs in the web app and in every worker).
    %% Defaults: heartbeat every 1 s, reaper every 2 s, visibility timeout 10 s.

    box Worker 1
        participant A as Consumer A
        participant HB as Heartbeat
    end
    participant DB as Postgres
    participant R as Reaper
    box Worker 2
        participant B as Consumer B
    end

    A->>DB: CLAIM
    DB-->>A: message 7 (processing, locked_by=A, attempts=1)

    loop every 1 s while A is working
        HB->>DB: heartbeat + RENEW_LEASE: locked_at = now() WHERE locked_by = A
    end

    Note over A: A crashes: killed from the UI, or the container gets SIGKILL.<br/>No ack, no nack
    Note over HB: A's lease is no longer renewed (if the whole worker died,<br/>its heartbeat stops too), so locked_at stops moving

    loop every 2 s
        R->>DB: REAP: processing AND locked_at older than 10 s (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)
        DB-->>R: nothing yet
    end

    Note over DB: 10 s after the last renewal
    R->>DB: REAP
    Note right of DB: message 7: status=pending, locked_by=NULL,<br/>last_error = lease expired (dead instead if attempts ≥ max_attempts)
    DB-->>R: [7]
    DB-)B: NOTIFY broker_messages (trigger: status changed to pending)

    B->>DB: CLAIM
    DB-->>B: message 7 (processing, locked_by=B, attempts=2)

    opt A was only frozen, not dead, and comes back
        A->>DB: ACK message 7 WHERE locked_by = A
        DB-->>A: 0 rows: the lease was lost, so the ack is ignored
        Note over A,B: The message was handled twice. Delivery is at-least-once:<br/>handlers must be idempotent
    end

    B->>DB: ACK message 7 WHERE locked_by = B
    DB-->>B: 1 row: message 7 done
